TigerSheets formula workspace: agent execution transcript excerpts
================================================================

PROVENANCE AND LIMITS
These are retrospective excerpts of command/output pairs actually observed in
the agent's execution-tool responses. The original runs were not redirected
to raw log files. This document is an execution transcript excerpt, NOT an
original raw stdout/stderr capture, and does not manufacture timestamps.

The standalone test was compiled/linked independently using:
  python3 /tmp/tigersheets-formula-workspace-build.py
That temporary helper compiled tests/formula_workspace_tests.cpp with
-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic and linked the existing build/ workspace libraries
plus the frozen formula-editor object. It did not mutate the shared build.
The build completed successfully without compiler warnings before each run
recorded below. The maintained test is now available through root CMake.

Working directory for all three commands:
  /workspace/tiger-sheets

RED 1: CELL COMPLETION TAB MUST NOT COMMIT
----------------------------------------
Stage: real MainWindow cell editor did not yet use FormulaLineEdit.
The binary at this stage contained the initial cell-completion regression.
Command actually executed:
  env QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen /tmp/tigersheets-formula-workspace-tests
Observed tool result: exit_code 1
Output excerpt (verbatim):
formula workspace test failed: autocomplete Tab must not commit incomplete =SUM to the canonical workbook

The test opened an actual cell editor with F2, typed =SUM, pressed Tab, and
compared the canonical snapshot before checking the resulting editor state.
This failed on the intended behavior: incomplete text was committed.

RED 2: WORKBOOK METADATA MUST SUPPLY COMPLETIONS
----------------------------------------------
Stage: the formula bar had built-in completion, but workbook names/functions
had not yet been connected to its completion context.
Command actually executed:
  env QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen /tmp/tigersheets-formula-workspace-tests workbook_context
Observed tool result: exit_code 1
Output excerpt (verbatim; preceding Qt offscreen notices omitted):
formula workspace test failed: set_metadata names must appear in nested formula-bar completion without a function parenthesis

The fixture applied set_metadata through WorksheetModel for names and enabled
VBA, recalculated, typed =IF(1,disco and pressed Tab. The expected pending
text was =IF(1,DiscountRate, without a function parenthesis or transaction.

FINAL INDEPENDENT GREEN
-----------------------
Stage: current integrated libraries, complete seven-scenario test, temporary
context-progression diagnostics removed, independently rebuilt and relinked.
Command actually executed:
  env QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen /tmp/tigersheets-formula-workspace-tests
Observed final tool result: exit_code 0
Output summary excerpt (verbatim; Qt offscreen notices omitted):
PASS cell_completion
PASS workbook_context
PASS bar_keyboard
PASS bar_mouse
PASS nested_hints
PASS escape
PASS unicode_f4
formula workspace tests passed

The final process returned output in multiple tool chunks; the summary above
was returned in the completion chunk. Qt's offscreen backend also printed
"This plugin does not support raise()" notices. Those notices are unrelated
to the assertions and are not represented here as failures or suppressed tests.

